1 NOTE Annie Pearl Battles was born at home at 1315 W. Grove, Tyler, Texas to Sallie Ma
2 CONC xine Battles and  Johnnie Calvin Battles. She attended T. J. Austin Elementary S
2 CONC chool (1st through 4th grades) 1949-  1953. She was voted queen of the school wh
2 CONC en she was in the second grade.  After leaving T. J. Austin, Annie attended Emme
2 CONC tt J. Scott Junior High School (5th grade) 1953-1954.  Annie’s mother, Sallie, a
2 CONC nd Annie’s stepfather, M. J. Hutcherson, moved to Los Angeles in January  1954. 
2 CONC Annie moved there when school was out in June. She attended the 66th Street Elem
2 CONC entary School  (6th grade) 1954-1955. After graduating from there, she attended 
2 CONC Thomas A. Edison Junior High  School, (7th grade) 1955-1956. She transferred to 
2 CONC John Adams Junior High School (7th through 9th  grades) 1956-1958. She was very 
2 CONC good at softball, and was voted athlete of the year in 1958. She  graduated from
2 CONC  John Adams then attended John C. Fremont High School (10th through 12th) grades
2 CONC   1958-1961.  After graduating from high school, Annie attended Los Angeles Trad
2 CONC e Technical College and went to  work for the Department of Public Social Servic
2 CONC es. She graduated from Control Data Institute in  November 1972 and went to work
2 CONC  for the California-American Water Company.  Annie met Bernard K. Richmond after
2 CONC  graduating from high school. She later married an old  schoolmate, Robert Lee H
2 CONC ale, January 15, 1977. Annie and Robert moved back to Texas in July 1986.  In Fe
2 CONC bruary 1988, Annie went to work for the Texas Department of Human Services.
