1 NOTE Lafane Battles, Sr. was a remarkable individual with a rich and diverse life sto
2 CONC ry. Born on February 7, 1935, in Smith County, Texas, he was the fourth child an
2 CONC d oldest son of J.T. and Cora Battles. His life journey came to an end on June 2
2 CONC 4, 2020.<br><br>Raised in Tyler, Texas, Lafane's early life was shaped by his wo
2 CONC rk at E. B. Baron Rose Nursery. His pursuit of work then led him to Ft. Worth, w
2 CONC here he joined his uncle Augustus Battles at Battles and Sons Cement Contractors
2 CONC . This experience laid the foundation for his strong work ethic, which he furthe
2 CONC r honed at Maxwell Steel Co. Later, he moved to Omaha, Nebraska, to work at Mast
2 CONC er Electronics, before eventually settling in Dallas, Texas. In Dallas, he embar
2 CONC ked on a diverse career path, working at Texas Bithulitc Construction Co, runnin
2 CONC g his own business, Battles Painting and Decorating Services, and contributing t
2 CONC o the Southwest Region Conference of Seventh-day Adventist. He also founded Enaf
2 CONC al and Associates, showcasing his expertise in construction, particularly in the
2 CONC  renovation of houses and churches in Ft. Worth and East Texas, spanning over 40
2 CONC  years.<br><br>Lafane was deeply involved in various business and community orga
2 CONC nizations. He was a charter member of the Better Business Bureau of East Texas a
2 CONC nd held memberships in the National Federation of Independent Business, Tyler Ch
2 CONC amber of Commerce, United States Chamber of Commerce, and Arp Chamber of Commerc
2 CONC e.<br><br>His personal life was as rich and full as his professional one. Lafane
2 CONC  was married to Kathryn Battles for 59 years, and together they raised a loving 
2 CONC family. Their children include Lafane Battles, Jr., Alafane Battles, and Lavonne
2 CONC  Richardson. He was a proud grandfather to seven grandchildren and a great-grand
2 CONC father to eleven great-grandchildren. Lafane's extensive family also included hi
2 CONC s siblings Pearlene Domino, Elizabeth Holmes, James Battles, Shirley Cobb, Claud
2 CONC ia Ferguson, Maurice Battles, and Fredrick Battles, along with his god-mother He
2 CONC len Harden and god-daughter Linda Singletary. His life was a tapestry of close f
2 CONC amily ties, deep friendships, and a committed involvement in his church communit
2 CONC y.<br><br>Lafane Battles, Sr.'s life was a testament to hard work, dedication to
2 CONC  family, and service to his community. His legacy lives on through his family, t
2 CONC he businesses he developed, and the many lives he touched.
