1 NOTE Obituary<br>Dorothy Caddell Wynn was born to the late Steve & Cleopatra Caddell 
2 CONC on March 22,1948 in Concord, Tx. She was joined by a twin, Martha Johnson.  She 
2 CONC later moved to Tyler Tx where she met Earnest L Wynn Sr & joined him in holy mat
2 CONC rimony on May 31,1966. Five children were born into this Union. They decided to 
2 CONC make Fort Worth Tx their permanent residence in 1968. She worked for Mrs. Bairds
2 CONC  bread for many years and later retired from Walmart. She was summoned peacefull
2 CONC y to her final resting place in Heaven on 02/01/2021 at Huguley Memorial hospita
2 CONC l. She was a kind, loving woman with a genuine spirit, yet very direct & thoroug
2 CONC h. She loved everyone and never saw our imperfections. She was filled with a lot
2 CONC  of wisdom and raised to serve God early on. <br>She is preceded in death by her
2 CONC  parents, Steve and Cleopatra Caddell; Mother-in-law, Parthenia McDonald; two br
2 CONC others, Charles & Carl Caddell; sister, Rose Mary Caddell Johnson; brother-in-la
2 CONC w, Edward Lee Wynn; grandson, Damian Jackson.<br>She leaves behind four siblings
2 CONC , Martha Johnson, Doris Ann Campbell (Eddie), Steve Caddell Jr & Peggy Elliott; 
2 CONC Children; Earnest Wynn Jr (Tamara), Darron Wynn, Kennth Wynn (Toni), Angela Wynn
2 CONC  and Michelle Wynn; 19 grandchildren and a host of great grandchildren and other
2 CONC  loved ones / friends.
